<title>UK: GUS shares gain amid bargain-hunting.</title>
<headline>GUS shares gain amid bargain-hunting.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Great Universal Stores Plc (GUS) rose on Thursday as investors bought the underperforming stock after recent falls and before it goes ex-dividend on Monday, traders said.</p>
<p>Seperately analysts at ABN AMRO Hoare Govett were said to have recommended switching into GUS and out of Boots Co Plc, though analysts at the brokerage declined comment.  </p>
<p>GUS shares were 11p higher at 622-1/2p by 1048 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;It's rallied because there's been a lot of profit-taking over the last few days and they are paying out a 7p (gross) dividend after Friday,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Boots was up 4p at 664p.</p>
<p>-- Paul Carrel, London newsroom</p>
</text>
